# Normalize line endings: LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# The project ships POSIX shell entry points (run.sh, deploy/seed.sh,
# backend/entrypoint.sh) that are executed directly and, for
# backend/entrypoint.sh, COPY'd into the API image as-is. A CRLF checkout
# (the Git for Windows default) breaks them with "/bin/bash^M: bad
# interpreter" or "$'\r': command not found", and ruff/prettier format
# checks fail on CRLF working trees. Forcing LF everywhere removes the
# whole class of failure.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts would need CRLF if any are ever added:
# *.bat text eol=crlf
# *.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalize, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
